          "text": "<h2>Use of the saber yankauer™ handheld illuminator in anterior approach total hip arthroplasty surgery<br>\n</h2>\n<p>A survey of leading orthopedic surgeons on the benefits for surgical precision, workflow efficiency &amp; patient safety</p>\n<p><b>Authors:</b>&nbsp;Joel Matta, John Masonis, MD, Anthony Carter, MD, David Homesley, MD, Tarun Bhargava, MD, Cass K Nakasone, MD, Hamid Redjal, MD, Charles DeCook, MD, Herrick Siegel, MD, J. Deal Cole, MD, Anthony Unger, MD</p>\n<p>Total hip arthroplasty (THA) is an established cost-effective treatment for arthritis of the hip joint. The anterior approach is becoming more popular among patients.<br>\n</p>\n",
